{"timestamp":"2026-08-05T18:58:11.582Z","ordinal":247,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019fd34a-53fe-7240-a2b9-8072b8a5aa77","call_id":"call_cKo6JZge21H3eJbOYyxPwpn9","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---\nname: plan-then-execute\ndescription: Crée un plan court, attend la validation explicite de l’utilisateur, puis exécute et vérifie la tâche. Utiliser quand l’utilisateur demande de planifier avant d’agir ou veut valider une opération non triviale.\n---\n\n# Plan puis exécution\n\n1. Comprendre l’objectif, le périmètre et les risques vérifiables.\n2. Donner un plan de 2 à 3 lignes et, si utile, les arbitrages importants.\n3. Attendre une validation explicite avant toute écriture, suppression, upload ou action externe.\n4. Après validation, exécuter le plan, vérifier le résultat et signaler les écarts.\n\n__ZENRAY__\n---\nname: zenrayprogress-context\ndescription: Load the current ZenRayProgress implementation context directly from its local repository. Use before implementing, debugging, reviewing, or operating ZenRayProgress instead of manually selecting project files.\n---\n\n# ZenRayProgress Context\n\nWork in `/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Productions/GithubProductions/ZenRayProgress`.\n\n1. Read `docs/INDEX-ERREURS-FEATURES.md` first, then `CLAUDE.md` and the current tail of `PROGRESS.md`.\n2. Inspect `git status --short`; preserve unrelated changes.\n3. Read the actual call sites and code for the requested feature with `rg`; do not rely on Memory or old plans when the repository differs.\n4. Reuse existing helpers and validate the real flow (build, endpoint, or browser) before claiming success.\n\n__DESIGN__\n---\nname: design-ux-ui-curves-liquidglass\ndescription: Contrat court pour les règles UI transverses ZenRay. Consulter seulement si Matthieu le nomme ou si la modification crée une nouvelle primitive visuelle partagée ; ne jamais retarder un correctif local.\n---\n\n# Liquid Glass ZenRay\n\n## Références vivantes\n\n- Doctrine append-only : `/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory/Design/Design1.md`.\n- Référence canonique V5 : `/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory/Design/ReusableComponentsButtons/glass-math-test.html`.\n- Preset par défaut : Liquid Glass Normal. Le code vivant du projet tranche les détails déjà implémentés.\n\n## Quand l'utiliser\n\n1. Lire l'index final de `Design1.md` et le composant réel ciblé.\n2. Ouvrir `glass-math-test.html` uniquement pour un bouton, une capsule, un panneau ou un lecteur glass.\n3. Construire, lancer le build, contrôler le rendu réel. Ne pas lancer un audit ni relire des thèmes sans rapport.\n\n## Recette V5\n\n- Fill : `rgba(255,255,255,.26)` ; `backdrop-filter: blur(22px) saturate(70%) brightness(1.28)`.\n- Grain SVG discret en overlay.\n- Rim : `inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.55), inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.55)` et une ombre douce.\n- `conic-gradient` est abandonné : il paraît chromé et se déforme sur les capsules et rectangles.\n- Cercle ou capsule : `border-radius:999px`. Carte et panneau : rayon fixe, même matière.\n- Le range natif garde son accessibilité, mais vit dans une capsule glass. Jamais de range visuellement nu.\n\n## Interaction\n\n- Clic, jamais hover, pour changer de niveau de navigation ou ouvrir une colonne Finder.\n- `0.15s` micro-interaction, `0.2–0.25s` standard, `0.3–0.35s` panneau ou grand déplacement, `cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)`.\n- Respecter `prefers-reduced-motion`.\n- Séparer une coque glass fixe de son scroller interne ; aucun backdrop-filter sur l'élément qui scrolle.\n\n## Documentation et sync\n\nAprès une règle nouvelle validée : append daté dans `Design1.md`, préciser la règle remplacée, puis lancer\n`~/.codex/skills/skill-sync/scripts/sync-skill.sh design-ux-ui-curves-liquidglass`.\n\n__KARPATHY__\n---\nname: karpathy-guidelines\ndescription: Behavioral guidelines to reduce common LLM coding mistakes. Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring code to avoid overcomplication, make surgical changes, surface assumptions, and define verifiable success criteria.\nlicense: MIT\n---\n\n# Karpathy Guidelines\n\nBehavioral guidelines to reduce common LLM coding mistakes, derived from [Andrej Karpathy's observations](https://x.com/karpathy/status/2015883857489522876) on LLM coding pitfalls.\n\n**Tradeoff:** These guidelines bias toward caution over speed. For trivial tasks, use judgment.\n\n## 1. Think Before Coding\n\n**Don't assume. Don't hide confusion. Surface tradeoffs.**\n\nBefore implementing:\n- State your assumptions explicitly. If uncertain, ask.\n- If multiple interpretations exist, present them - don't pick silently.\n- If a simpler approach exists, say so. Push back when warranted.\n- If something is unclear, stop. Name what's confusing. Ask.\n\n## 2. Simplicity First\n\n**Minimum code that solves the problem. Nothing speculative.**\n\n- No features beyond what was asked.\n- No abstractions for single-use code.\n- No \"flexibility\" or \"configurability\" that wasn't requested.\n- No error handling for impossible scenarios.\n- If you write 200 lines and it could be 50, rewrite it.\n\nAsk yourself: \"Would a senior engineer say this is overcomplicated?\" If yes, simplify.\n\n## 3. Surgical Changes\n\n**Touch only what you must. Clean up only your own mess.**\n\nWhen editing existing code:\n- Don't \"improve\" adjacent code, comments, or formatting.\n- Don't refactor things that aren't broken.\n- Match existing style, even if you'd do it differently.\n- If you notice unrelated dead code, mention it - don't delete it.\n\nWhen your changes create orphans:\n- Remove imports/variables/functions that YOUR changes made unused.\n- Don't remove pre-existing dead code unless asked.\n\nThe test: Every changed line should trace directly to the user's request.\n\n## 4. Goal-Driven Execution\n\n**Define success criteria. Loop until verified.**\n\nTransform tasks into verifiable goals:\n- \"Add validation\" → \"Write tests for invalid inputs, then make them pass\"\n- \"Fix the bug\" → \"Write a test that reproduces it, then make it pass\"\n- \"Refactor X\" → \"Ensure tests pass before and after\"\n\nFor multi-step tasks, state a brief plan:\n```\n1. [Step] → verify: [check]\n2. [Step] → verify: [check]\n3. [Step] → verify: [check]\n```\n\nStrong success criteria let you loop independently. Weak criteria (\"make it work\") require constant clarification.\n\n__STATUS__\n M PROGRESS.md\n M docs/zenraymedia/README.md\n M src/zenraymedia/MediaApp.jsx\n M src/zenraymedia/MediaApp.test.jsx\n M src/zenraymedia/compile.js\n M src/zenraymedia/layers.js\n M src/zenraymedia/layers.test.js\n M src/zenraymedia/media.css\n?? .wrangler/\n?? docs/zenraymedia/audits/\n?? state.json\n\n__PLAN_STATUS__\n\n__PLAN_HASHES__\n3d2c164ee6a97ad57e8e47b96506f6b6c76870b08f79601f09354e468cd4a4b8  src/create/PlanBoard.jsx\n6961113a25dc237008bbd2d9159093f844221a1c0223ea3556dbea4270dc8dc5  src/create/PlanBoard.css\nd5593d0d3a82ff6eee409960be6f1e88366ac2847ab5495045186a5ed6bdc79e  src/create/planScore.js\n9313e67a87d0ebc1db75cf9e9cc424b804a8b0d9cb1be4962937fe9b264bc152  src/create/planScore.test.js\n\n__PLAN_MTIMES__\n2026-08-01 03:55:12 src/create/PlanBoard.jsx\n2026-08-01 03:55:12 src/create/PlanBoard.css\n2026-08-01 03:55:12 src/create/planScore.js\n2026-08-01 03:55:12 src/create/planScore.test.js\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd34a-19f9-75f2-9218-8dd24e958a07"}}}
